{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381679-v5-speculation-alternate-rules-in-pg","id":1381679,"title":"[V5, +, Speculation] Alternate Rules in PG","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-15T10:06:12-07:00","id":1381679,"title":"[V5, +, Speculation] Alternate Rules in PG","content":"So we were initially told the player's guide would have some alternate takes and additional rules to adapt more playstyles. We have also been told that the PG won't override the core book, it will work alongside it. So I'm curious... what alternate rules/ways to make certain settings would you want to see in the PG?<br /> <br /> For me, it comes down to adding optional methods to do stuff:<br /> * Add a PC creation guide/option for Elders of 8th Gen through 6th Gen (XP to build, extra Advantages and Flaws), along with a way for Elders to have more powers without needing 6+ Disciplines; breadth instead of height.<br /> * Rule for non-Human Touchstones and Rituals and/or Loresheets to represent Path ethos.<br /> * Ways to tweak weapons without it just being scads more bonus dice, or getting into minutiae of aiming better. <br /> * Notes for possible replacement Skills for different play eras (Mythic Past, Dark Ages, Victorian).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T10:47:54-07:00","id":1381700,"title":"","content":"* I hope for some definite rules for non-Human Touchstones.<br /> * I hope for some ideas for Paths.<br /> * +5 Disciplines to be possessed by Elders.<br /> * Rules for Sabbat play.<br /> * Tzimisce rules for play.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T14:19:02-07:00","id":1381978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381679-v5-speculation-alternate-rules-in-pg?p=1381700#post1381700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* I hope for some definite rules for non-Human Touchstones.<br /> * I hope for some ideas for Paths.<br /> * +5 Disciplines to be possessed by Elders.<br /> * Rules for Sabbat play.<br /> * Tzimisce rules for play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could have sworn that I saw a specific reason why they capped the attributes at 5 somewhere... some mathematical calculation regarding success probabilities. Maybe I imagined it. I can't honestly say I'm too fussed about it, anyway. The niggle I always had with the old edition was that some elders were practically mini-Cthulhus in power. The new rules junk that somewhat and keep the bit I find interesting (centuries of experience, convoluted backstories). That said, giving elders options like multiple powers at the same Discipline level or enhanced Backgrounds would be nice.<br /> <br /> I'd like something to make the Touchstone/Conviction link optional.<br /> Vampire Touchstones would help with centuries-old coteries if you wanted to play long-term chronicles. The Gentleman's Guide V5 intro on the subject hinted at something of the sort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T14:43:15-07:00","id":1381982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JezMiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381679-v5-speculation-alternate-rules-in-pg?p=1381978#post1381978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could have sworn that I saw a specific reason why they capped the attributes at 5 somewhere... some mathematical calculation regarding success probabilities. Maybe I imagined it. I can't honestly say I'm too fussed about it, anyway. The niggle I always had with the old edition was that some elders were practically mini-Cthulhus in power. The new rules junk that somewhat and keep the bit I find interesting (centuries of experience, convoluted backstories). That said, giving elders options like multiple powers at the same Discipline level or enhanced Backgrounds would be nice.<br /> <br /> I'd like something to make the Touchstone/Conviction link optional.<br /> Vampire Touchstones would help with centuries-old coteries if you wanted to play long-term chronicles. The Gentleman's Guide V5 intro on the subject hinted at something of the sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, elders of the 7th gen or lower as it is can have a dice pool of 17 with blood surge for disciplines which comes to, roughly 9.5 successes, 6+ disciplines would up that to 10. As a difficulty 7 is supposed to be nearly impossible well. Yeah it would break the system.<br /> <br /> More on topic, alternate XP rules, alternative combat rules, expanded disciplines would all be nice to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T02:36:56-07:00","id":1382089,"title":"","content":"I mean, with Mithras' stats in the Fall of London, the Ventrue traits, and the Cult of Mithras Loresheet all taken into account, it could be argued that some of Mithras' rolls would have 20-22 die pre-Blood Surge (Charisma 5, Persuasion 5, Presence 5, being able to just give any Kindred with his vitae 3 extra die on Presence checks, +1/2 die on Social tests from Appearance, Intense Sanguine Resonance, Specialties in Persuasion and Intimidation), with 24-26 following the Blood Surge (Blood Potency 8). I know he's a 4th Generation, but I think the point of Elders is to kind of be game-breaking. There's a reason Blood Potency above 5 isn't really intended for gameplay, but the rest of that stuff could be achieved within reasonable limits of the game. If you start as an Ancilla, it could be achieved pretty easily. You could start out with Presence 4 (Clan with Presence at 2, Siren to bump it to 3, 20 XP to 4), Persuasion 5 (Specialist, 15 XP), Stunning (4 Advantage dots), a Persuasion Specialty in Seduction (Siren), and the other 3 Advantage dots going to the Cult of Mithras. Getting to Charisma 5, Presence 5, and Cult of Mithras 5 would only take 56 XP and you'd literally be able to use that many die with your Seduction tests as an Ancilla (23 with the Blood Surge under certain conditions).<br /> <br /> This was a bit of a tangent, mind me. I do hope the Player's Guide at least introduces Dark Thaumaturgy. I won't what they'd call it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26012-niarobi","name":"Niarobi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T02:46:55-07:00","id":1382093,"title":"","content":"<i>* Rules for non-Human Touchstones.</i><br /> <i>* Mechanics for Paths.</i><br /> <i>* +5 Disciplines</i><br /> <i>* Rules for Sabbat and Ashirra and Laibon play.</i><br /> <i>* Tzimisce rules for play. ( Bloodlines? Maybe Rules for Build a Bloodline that go beyond Loresheets?)<br /> * Alternatives to Hunger Dice.<br /> * Alternative Discipline Powers.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T02:56:13-07:00","id":1382095,"title":"","content":"a core system actually arranged to explain the systems.<br /> <br /> Seriously, A book laid out/designed professionally","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2782,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2782-pittmonkey","user":"Pittmonkey","date":". 04-17-2020, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2782-pittmonkey","name":"Pittmonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2782_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T03:28:04-07:00","id":1382106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JezMiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381679-v5-speculation-alternate-rules-in-pg?p=1381978#post1381978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could have sworn that I saw a specific reason why they capped the attributes at 5 somewhere... some mathematical calculation regarding success probabilities. Maybe I imagined it. I can't honestly say I'm too fussed about it, anyway. The niggle I always had with the old edition was that some elders were practically mini-Cthulhus in power. The new rules junk that somewhat and keep the bit I find interesting (centuries of experience, convoluted backstories). That said, giving elders options like multiple powers at the same Discipline level or enhanced Backgrounds would be nice.<br /> <br /> I'd like something to make the Touchstone/Conviction link optional.<br /> Vampire Touchstones would help with centuries-old coteries if you wanted to play long-term chronicles. The Gentleman's Guide V5 intro on the subject hinted at something of the sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you'd need something separate like, &quot;Elder Blood Sorcery&quot; or &quot;Elder Potence&quot; completely separate from the original.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T17:15:31-07:00","id":1382266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pittmonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381679-v5-speculation-alternate-rules-in-pg?p=1382095#post1382095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a core system actually arranged to explain the systems.<br /> <br /> Seriously, A book laid out/designed professionally</div> </div> </div> </div>Which part are you having trouble with? If you're not able to understand the book I'm sure some people here would be pleased to help you until you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T18:11:40-07:00","id":1382645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381679-v5-speculation-alternate-rules-in-pg?p=1382266#post1382266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which part are you having trouble with? If you're not able to understand the book I'm sure some people here would be pleased to help you until you do.</div> </div> </div> </div> Even once one comes to &quot;understand&quot; the rules and the game despite the poor organization and layout, the fact remains that old RPG books <i>look </i>the way they do for a reason--they're constantly being open, perused, and referenced for one rule or other that someone/everyone can't remember exactly--the ST screen is great, but it's not exhaustive. The more poor the layout of the book, the harder it is to find things, and the more it potentially slows down play.<br /> <br /> It's not unfair to ask that a book of rules--like any reference material--be organized in a way that maximizes the user's ability to quickly find and review whatever rule. What's more, it's not like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2782-pittmonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2782_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2782\" data-vbnamecard=\"2782\">Pittmonkey</a> is the first person to bemoan the books poor layout. Credit where due: it's pretty as hell--but keeping it real, it's also pretty difficult to navigate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T18:20:09-07:00","id":1382650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381679-v5-speculation-alternate-rules-in-pg?p=1381700#post1381700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* I hope for some definite rules for non-Human Touchstones.<br /> * I hope for some ideas for Paths.<br /> * +5 Disciplines to be possessed by Elders.<br /> * Rules for Sabbat play.<br /> * Tzimisce rules for play.</div> </div> </div> </div>We share a similar wishlist, but Id also like to see conversion rules for previous editions, (though Paradox could also release these for free). Id also like the new PG to have rules for historical play, (e.g., skills for different historical time periods, Dark Ages).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/337-joe","name":"Joe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T18:15:34-07:00","id":1382865,"title":"","content":"I still think they failed without disciplines going past 5 so that's an obvious one, but the more I think about it stats and skills capping at 5 is nice. I may do that for V20 games. There have been lots of times reading the description of the 1-5 skill levels do make having a 8 or 9 seem silly. I remember all the Dark Age level 6 's in the main book just saying legend or something. A 6 is easy to picture but by 8 or 9 say crafts computer skill or academics or law... How far can these things really improve over world renown leader in the field. I think the stats and abilities capping at five is the one improvement V5 makes but disciplines capping at 5 is just asking for trouble when it comes to big bads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T18:48:08-07:00","id":1382868,"title":"","content":"The only way for disciplines to be allowed to go above five is with a complete rework of the discipline system where discipline rolls do not add the dots in the discipline to a roll. As it stands, the average 7th gen has with 5 in the attribute and 5 in the discipline, a minimum of 11 dice, and a maximum (At max blood potency) of 17 dice. 18 if you use the intense resonance which means it would be an average difficulty of 9. You would need at least 5 dice to hope to meet their average roll, but. Even a maxed out neonate (So 5 Attribute + 5 Resisting skill + 1 Discipline bonus and + 2 Blood Surge) has the bare minimum to meet said 7th generation elder who just awoke from a centuries long torpor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T09:41:32-07:00","id":1382985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381679-v5-speculation-alternate-rules-in-pg?p=1382650#post1382650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We share a similar wishlist, but Id also like to see conversion rules for previous editions, (though Paradox could also release these for free). Id also like the new PG to have rules for historical play, (e.g., skills for different historical time periods, Dark Ages).</div> </div> </div> </div> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a><br /> <br /> <br /> We've been told by the line devs that WW has no plans for traits to go above 5, and we've been told by line devs that there won't be Sabbat-playable anything in the PG (and the words 'too Sabbat' were mentioned when it was said in an interview that the Tzimisce were kicked back for rewrites and might not be in the book due to that, so we know that's a true statement).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381679-v5-speculation-alternate-rules-in-pg?p=1382868#post1382868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only way for disciplines to be allowed to go above five is with a complete rework of the discipline system where discipline rolls do not add the dots in the discipline to a roll. As it stands, the average 7th gen has with 5 in the attribute and 5 in the discipline, a minimum of 11 dice, and a maximum (At max blood potency) of 17 dice. 18 if you use the intense resonance which means it would be an average difficulty of 9. You would need at least 5 dice to hope to meet their average roll, but. Even a maxed out neonate (So 5 Attribute + 5 Resisting skill + 1 Discipline bonus and + 2 Blood Surge) has the bare minimum to meet said 7th generation elder who just awoke from a centuries long torpor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did some numbers calculations in a discussion about this the other day, and largely the scale down is an issue of how the dice function. I think, even without a Resonance, I ended up with 31 dice for a full-powered BP8 vampire with an assumed stat/skill/Discipline of 7. Even with stats capped at 5 it's still crazy (Toreador with BP 8 and Awe active, assuming max traits and Presence 7: 5 stat, 5 skill, spec +1, Presence 7, DPB 4 = 22. If Torrie blood surges that's 26 dice. If Torrie has Striking and it applies, that's +2 for 28. Not to mention anything else you could attempt to try to stack on it from Loresheets, Resonance, etc.)<br /> <br /> And that's not even accounting for general scale overall, such as Potence above 5; with Potence 6 you need 2 margin to outright kill/torpor anyone that doesn't have Fortitude. Elder Brujah with Fist of Caine, Potence 6, Strength 5 Brawl 5 Spec +1. That's 11 dice to do agg, and you only need 2 margin over your opponent to outright destroy a character with Stamina 5 (as 8 is the maximum health levels).<br /> <br /> What elders need is either 1. something locked to being purchased via high BP (an option I'm not too fond of, but will entertain ideas on) that needs to not just scale upward and stack on more dice adders, or the ability to purchase more powers, especially with V5's design focusing on breadth of powers rather than height (which is my preferred option for elders).<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 04-21-2020, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T10:59:11-07:00","id":1383002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381679-v5-speculation-alternate-rules-in-pg?p=1382985#post1382985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">especially with V5's design focusing on breadth of powers rather than height (which is my preferred option for elders).<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my go-to when it comes to not even Elder Elders but like Primogen and such. You can expect a run-of-the-mill vampire of any clans to be set to their clan Disciplines (and rarely more than 3 dots in any particular one) but the Brujah Primogen is going to have Auspex so you can't just sneak away, the Nosferatu is going to have Dominate so it can cover up breaches of walking around, and the Ventrue is going to have Potence for when conversation breaks down. A mark of a strong vampire is one who has not only perfected their clan's style of business but covered their weak points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T17:40:58-07:00","id":1383059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381679-v5-speculation-alternate-rules-in-pg?p=1383002#post1383002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is my go-to when it comes to not even Elder Elders but like Primogen and such. You can expect a run-of-the-mill vampire of any clans to be set to their clan Disciplines (and rarely more than 3 dots in any particular one) but the Brujah Primogen is going to have Auspex so you can't just sneak away, the Nosferatu is going to have Dominate so it can cover up breaches of walking around, and the Ventrue is going to have Potence for when conversation breaks down. A mark of a strong vampire is one who has not only perfected their clan's style of business but covered their weak points.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> By breadth I more meant allowing Elders of 8th or lower Gen to buy more than just the standard 5 powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T12:45:38-07:00","id":1383995,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As far as Elder PCs go... I'm not opposed to it. I wouldn't allow PC Generation to go lower than 8- after all, older editions made Generation an Advantage you had to buy, and IIRC that was capped at 5 dots- and set the max age so that Elder Characters can't have been older than neonates when the Convention of Thorns went down.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">From a gameplay perspective, I think 9th generation hits the sweet-spot of giving the PCs way more power than most of the other local Kindred, but still not being the biggest, baddest players in town, but they aren't engaging in the same petty errand-running that a PC coterie of fledglings would. A fledgling game plays very differently from a neonate game, plays very differently from an ancilla game, plays very differently from an elder game. </span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Mechanically, drop the PC humanity by another dot, give them a couple more dots to allocate Advantages and Flaws, and then give them 80 XP to spend on whatever they want.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T15:16:54-07:00","id":1384279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381679-v5-speculation-alternate-rules-in-pg?p=1382985#post1382985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span><br /> <br /> <br /> We've been told by the line devs that WW has no plans for traits to go above 5, and we've been told by line devs that there won't be Sabbat-playable anything in the PG (and the words 'too Sabbat' were mentioned when it was said in an interview that the Tzimisce were kicked back for rewrites and might not be in the book due to that, so we know that's a true statement).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I did some numbers calculations in a discussion about this the other day, and largely the scale down is an issue of how the dice function. I think, even without a Resonance, I ended up with 31 dice for a full-powered BP8 vampire with an assumed stat/skill/Discipline of 7. Even with stats capped at 5 it's still crazy (Toreador with BP 8 and Awe active, assuming max traits and Presence 7: 5 stat, 5 skill, spec +1, Presence 7, DPB 4 = 22. If Torrie blood surges that's 26 dice. If Torrie has Striking and it applies, that's +2 for 28. Not to mention anything else you could attempt to try to stack on it from Loresheets, Resonance, etc.)<br /> <br /> And that's not even accounting for general scale overall, such as Potence above 5; with Potence 6 you need 2 margin to outright kill/torpor anyone that doesn't have Fortitude. Elder Brujah with Fist of Caine, Potence 6, Strength 5 Brawl 5 Spec +1. That's 11 dice to do agg, and you only need 2 margin over your opponent to outright destroy a character with Stamina 5 (as 8 is the maximum health levels).<br /> <br /> What elders need is either 1. something locked to being purchased via high BP (an option I'm not too fond of, but will entertain ideas on) that needs to not just scale upward and stack on more dice adders, or the ability to purchase more powers, especially with V5's design focusing on breadth of powers rather than height (which is my preferred option for elders).<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait the Tzimisce were too Sabbat? What were they expecting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T15:28:00-07:00","id":1384283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381679-v5-speculation-alternate-rules-in-pg?p=1384279#post1384279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait the Tzimisce were too Sabbat? What were they expecting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something that lines up with their vision of 'Sabbat are not playable yet, and removal of sect-locking the clans'. I would think Modi was probably given some overall guidelines (as WW has mentioned setting bibles and they are in charge of all QC) and what they wrote for those was still too Sabbat-focused (as there aren't any announcements for a Sabbat book yet, and the core stuff we've seen has introduced a lot of interesting plot to decouple clans from being locked to only playing in one sect). So kicked back to fix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T08:53:55-07:00","id":1384421,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The easiest way to decouple the Tzimisce from the Sabbat, IMO, is to have them come to view the Sabbat as a failed experiment. The Tzimisce were always the spiritual pillar of the Sabbat. If you think the senseless sacrifice of the Gehenna Crusade was a hit to the morale of the pragmatic Lasombra, imagine how devastated the Tzimisce are: dozens of Sabbat dying to subdue a single Methuselah, only for that Methuselah to subsume the will of the poor sap granted the privilege of diablerizing it. The Sword of Caine is devolving into a horde of mindless beasts. This isn't evolution, this is banal regression and subjugation to the Elders of the worst sort imaginable. The dream of the Sabbat has become a nightmarish parody of itself. </span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Tzimisce who have not turned into Methuselah meat puppets or wights pack up and flee for their ancestral homeland of Transylvania. The Fiends try to collect their thoughts, and it isn't long before bitter recriminations start to get thrown around. Who should roll up but, you guessed it, Dracula. He lays the blame for everything at the feet of Kupala: he posits that Kupala's breaking of their blood bonds was false hope, a plot between the demon and the Eldest. Desperate for revenge, the Tzimisce join Dracula in tracking down and destroying Kupala's physical form. Dracula absorbs a bit of Kupala's essence, and he is declared the Voivode of Voivodes, the supreme leader and ultimate authority of the newly reunified Tzimisce.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Politically, I can actually see the Tzimisce favoring the Anarch Movement: I have trouble seeing members of the former Old Clan accepting the idea of somebody having authority over them (besides Dracula) as would happen in the Camarilla, and the former Sabbat Tzimisce will probably choose the Anarchs as a &quot;next best thing&quot; kind of situation, and maybe even try to steer the Anarchs back towards the ideals of the First Anarch Revolt. In any case, I can see the Tzimisce harboring a nice healthy grudge against the Lasombra for siding with the Camarilla, and for turning on their former allies so readily when it suited them, even if a Fiend does decide to join the Camarilla as well.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T08:58:15-07:00","id":1384422,"title":"","content":"It's what happened to CULTS OF THE BLOOD GODS apparently where the write up for the Church of Caine was entirely about the Sabbat and their religion.<br /> <br /> Then White Wolf had to step in and go, &quot;Uh, guys, this is not a Sabbat book. It's for Anarchs, Cammies, Hecata, and Independent players. Rewrite it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hence the Cainite Heresy is back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T09:38:28-07:00","id":1384431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381679-v5-speculation-alternate-rules-in-pg?p=1384421#post1384421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The easiest way to decouple the Tzimisce from the Sabbat, IMO, is to have them come to view the Sabbat as a failed experiment. The Tzimisce were always the spiritual pillar of the Sabbat. If you think the senseless sacrifice of the Gehenna Crusade was a hit to the morale of the pragmatic Lasombra, imagine how devastated the Tzimisce are: dozens of Sabbat dying to subdue a single Methuselah, only for that Methuselah to subsume the will of the poor sap granted the privilege of diablerizing it. The Sword of Caine is devolving into a horde of mindless beasts. This isn't evolution, this is banal regression and subjugation to the Elders of the worst sort imaginable. The dream of the Sabbat has become a nightmarish parody of itself. </span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Tzimisce who have not turned into Methuselah meat puppets or wights pack up and flee for their ancestral homeland of Transylvania. The Fiends try to collect their thoughts, and it isn't long before bitter recriminations start to get thrown around. Who should roll up but, you guessed it, Dracula. He lays the blame for everything at the feet of Kupala: he posits that Kupala's breaking of their blood bonds was false hope, a plot between the demon and the Eldest. Desperate for revenge, the Tzimisce join Dracula in tracking down and destroying Kupala's physical form. Dracula absorbs a bit of Kupala's essence, and he is declared the Voivode of Voivodes, the supreme leader and ultimate authority of the newly reunified Tzimisce.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Politically, I can actually see the Tzimisce favoring the Anarch Movement: I have trouble seeing members of the former Old Clan accepting the idea of somebody having authority over them (besides Dracula) as would happen in the Camarilla, and the former Sabbat Tzimisce will probably choose the Anarchs as a &quot;next best thing&quot; kind of situation, and maybe even try to steer the Anarchs back towards the ideals of the First Anarch Revolt. In any case, I can see the Tzimisce harboring a nice healthy grudge against the Lasombra for siding with the Camarilla, and for turning on their former allies so readily when it suited them, even if a Fiend does decide to join the Camarilla as well.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like this and it lines up largely with what I was going to be doing for parts of my Tzimisce homebrew. I may steal a bit of it for wording, with your permission?<br /> <br /> Aside, we have very little other information on the Tzimisce, other than we have seen consistent use of the moniker Old Clan, such as the current Prince of Tokyo, and they'll have Protean (a character learned Protean from a Tzimisce lover). Anything else right now is hidden behind an NDA lock from the playtesting, and any of that may be thrown out the door anyway. So we'll have to be patient, but I hope we get something creative and also something that hints at the state of the Sabbat as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T11:34:30-07:00","id":1384458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381679-v5-speculation-alternate-rules-in-pg?p=1384431#post1384431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this and it lines up largely with what I was going to be doing for parts of my Tzimisce homebrew. I may steal a bit of it for wording, with your permission?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure! Always happy to collaborate. <br /> <br /> As for the Sabbat... yeah. The hints that we're getting from current V5 lore is that the Camarilla and Ashirra are <i>at best</i> stalling the Sabbat. At some point their efforts are going to fail, and the Return of the Sabbat is going to be scary, even before the possibility of forgotten Methuselahs and even Antes walking around incognito. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T12:52:43-07:00","id":1384478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381679-v5-speculation-alternate-rules-in-pg?p=1384422#post1384422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's what happened to CULTS OF THE BLOOD GODS apparently where the write up for the Church of Caine was entirely about the Sabbat and their religion.<br /> <br /> Then White Wolf had to step in and go, &quot;Uh, guys, this is not a Sabbat book. It's for Anarchs, Cammies, Hecata, and Independent players. Rewrite it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hence the Cainite Heresy is back.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> the 'the devs aren't screaming hate at the fanbase' claim is looking thinner and thinner with every revelation like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T12:57:27-07:00","id":1384482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381679-v5-speculation-alternate-rules-in-pg?p=1384478#post1384478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 'the devs aren't screaming hate at the fanbase' claim is looking thinner and thinner with every revelation like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we can also do away with speculation on conspiracies against fans.<br /> <br /> But I would be interested in why you think them not doing the Sabbat before their own book is a bad thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T14:01:28-07:00","id":1384499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381679-v5-speculation-alternate-rules-in-pg?p=1384482#post1384482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we can also do away with speculation on conspiracies against fans.<br /> <br /> But I would be interested in why you think them not doing the Sabbat before their own book is a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I have stopped believing a Sabbat book will come, or that if one eventually does appear that it will represent anything of what I loved about them (for instance Paths just flat don't work, even with none human touchstones, and yea this was tested, they need the granularity of a Heirachy to work) and big chunks of the sect are being torn away, neutered, mutilated and given to the cam and Anarchs, after the entire sect swallowed the idiot ball to make a comment on foreign involvement in the Middle East.<br /> <br /> All we could reasonably hope for was a broken up release of just enough rules to cobble together something semi usable, but WW are denying even that, apparently they want Anarchs and Cam to be the only things playable (with the Independents also being swallowed by the Anarchs for reasons that again make zero sense, so even that escape is denied players.)<br /> <br /> That looks am awful lot like they have in mind exactly one way to play, with the characters of the playtest making it clear exactly what the ideal is (and no I didn't then, and don't know believe the spin about us misinterpreted descriptions and mistranslation of 'kids')<br /> <br /> That's before we get onto the other problems, such as no disciplines above 5, no more than 5 powers per discipline including amalgams, the hunger dice system in it's game destroying entirety, chronicle tenets, blood potency as a concept etc etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-28-2020, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T14:10:03-07:00","id":1384502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381679-v5-speculation-alternate-rules-in-pg?p=1384499#post1384499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because I have stopped believing a Sabbat book will come, or that if one eventually does appear that it will represent anything of what I loved about them (for instance Paths just flat don't work, even with none human touchstones, and yea this was tested, they need the granularity of a Heirachy to work) and big chunks of the sect are being torn away, neutered, mutilated and given to the cam and Anarchs, after the entire sect swallowed the idiot ball to make a comment on foreign involvement in the Middle East.<br /> <br /> All we could reasonably hope for was a broken up release of just enough rules to cobble together something semi usable, but WW are denying even that, apparently they want Anarchs and Cam to be the only things playable (with the Independents also being swallowed by the Anarchs for reasons that again make zero sense, so even that escape is denied players.)<br /> <br /> That looks am awful lot like they have in mind exactly one way to play, with the characters of the playtest making it clear exactly what the ideal is (and no I didn't then, and don't know believe the spin about us misinterpreted descriptions and mistranslation of 'kids')</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing stops you from playing the game the way you want to play. The only thing that stops you from the story that you want is you and your gamingn group.<br /> <br /> This has been the way it was from the very first edition of this game. Didn't want Lodin dead, he wasn't; wanted the sabbat as boogee men, they were; wanted Viscisitude to be something from earth rather than outerspace, it was; didn't want a cure for Vamirism, there wasn't one; didn't want the avatar storm to exist, never happened; heck, didn't want he world to end, it didn't.<br /> <br /> The only thing that stops you is you. blaming others is not productive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T14:13:18-07:00","id":1384504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381679-v5-speculation-alternate-rules-in-pg?p=1384502#post1384502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing stops you from playing the game the way you want to play. The only thing that stops you from the story that you want is you and your gamingn group.<br /> <br /> This has been the way it was from the very first edition of this game. Didn't want Lodin dead he wasn't wanted the sabbat as boogee men they were wanted Viscisitude to be something from earth rather than outerspace it was, didn't want a cure for Vamirism there wasn't one, didn't want the avatar storm to exist never happened, heck, didn't want he world to end it didn't.<br /> <br /> The only thing that stops you is you. blaming others is not productive.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that helps a discussion on current canon how? Sure I can head canon as much as I like, what ever I like, but then that's not a setting I will get to play, or a game that is supported by the rules, and of it is not supported by the published rules it doesn't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T14:13:48-07:00","id":1384505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381679-v5-speculation-alternate-rules-in-pg?p=1384499#post1384499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because I have stopped believing a Sabbat book will come, or that if one eventually does appear that it will represent anything of what I loved about them (for instance Paths just flat don't work, even with none human touchstones, and yea this was tested, they need the granularity of a Heirachy to work) and big chunks of the sect are being torn away, neutered, mutilated and given to the cam and Anarchs, after the entire sect swallowed the idiot ball to make a comment on foreign involvement in the Middle East.<br /> <br /> All we could reasonably hope for was a broken up release of just enough rules to cobble together something semi usable, but WW are denying even that, apparently they want Anarchs and Cam to be the only things playable (with the Independents also being swallowed by the Anarchs for reasons that again make zero sense, so even that escape is denied players.)<br /> <br /> That looks am awful lot like they have in mind exactly one way to play, with the characters of the playtest making it clear exactly what the ideal is (and no I didn't then, and don't know believe the spin about us misinterpreted descriptions and mistranslation of 'kids')<br /> <br /> That's before we get onto the other problems, such as no disciplines above 5, no more than 5 powers per discipline including amalgams, the hunger dice system in it's game destroying entirety, chronicle tenets, blood potency as a concept etc etc</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I was just asking about the Sabbat but thanks for sharing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381679-v5-speculation-alternate-rules-in-pg?p=1384504#post1384504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that helps a discussion on current canon how? Sure I can head canon as much as I like, what ever I like, but then that's not a setting I will get to play, or a game that is supported by the rules, and of it is not supported by the published rules it doesn't exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>